  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "hook": "Can a circuit multiply voltage without using a single transformer?",
  "question": "A series RLC circuit has a resonant frequency of 1000 radians per second and a quality factor of 10. What is its half-power bandwidth?",
  "options": [
   "100 radians per second",
   "10000 radians per second",
   "10 radians per second",
   "50 radians per second"
  ],
  "correctIndex": 0,
  "answerLine": "The half-power bandwidth is 100 radians per second.",
  "explanation": [
   "In a series resonant circuit, the quality factor measures the sharpness of the resonant response peak.",
   "By definition, quality factor equals resonant angular frequency divided by the total half-power bandwidth.",
   "The half-power bandwidth represents the frequency band where power dissipation remains at least half maximum.",
   "Rearranging this standard formula gives bandwidth equal to resonant frequency divided by the quality factor."
  ],
  "funFact": "At resonance, the voltages across the inductor and capacitor can easily exceed the supply voltage by tenfold!",
  "outro": "Master your resonant circuit formulas and crack your upcoming Assistant Engineer exams with full confidence!",
